[s0l0!-header][h1]The if Statement [/h1][/s0l0!-header] 
Well done! You’re making great progress. On to module 3!

Often when we write code, we want to perform different actions based on different conditions.

And this is where [b]conditional statements[/b] come in. 

There are a bunch of different conditionals, to cover, but we’re starting with one of the most useful: "if"

We use [b]if [/b]to specify a block of code that we want to be executed if a specified condition is true.[code format="js" ]if (condition) {
   statements
}[/code]
The statements will only be executed if the specified condition is [b]true[/b]. Let’s take a look at an example:
[s0l0!-header][/s0l0!-header] [code format="js" codeId="660"]var myNum1 = 7;
var myNum2 = 10;
[b]if [/b](myNum1 < myNum2) {
   alert("JavaScript is easy to learn.");
}[/code]
[s0l0!-header][b]Result:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [img id="2751" width="100%"]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
You can see from the example above, we’ve used the JavaScript [b]alert()[/b] to generate a popup alert box that contains the information inside the parentheses.[/note]

