[s0l0!-header][h1]The if Statement[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Here’s a little more detail on the if statement.

This is an example of a [b]false [/b]conditional statement:[code format="js" codeId="4840"]var myNum1 = 7;
var myNum2 = 10;
if (myNum1 [b]>[/b] myNum2) {
   alert("JavaScript is easy to learn.");
}[/code]
Because the condition evaluates to false, the alert statement gets skipped and the program continues with the line after the if statement's closing curly brace.
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
[b]if[/b] is in lowercase letters. Uppercase letters (If or IF) won’t work.[/note]
